    "problem_statement": "Path.remove() method returns None instead of self\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `Path.remove()` method is supposed to return `self` to allow method chaining, but it's currently returning `None` which breaks the fluent interface.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport furl\n\n# This should work but fails\np = furl.Path('a/b/c/')\nresult = p.remove(['b'])\nprint(result)  # Prints: None (should print the Path object)\n\n# Method chaining is broken\np = furl.Path('a/b/c/')\ntry:\n    p.remove(['b']).remove(['a'])  # AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'remove'\nexcept AttributeError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n\nExpected behavior: `remove()` should return the Path instance to enable method chaining like other Path methods."
  }
